Deepwyrm uses component-aware licensing.

Unless otherwise indicated, Deepwyrm source code is licensed under the GNU General Public License version 2 or, at your option, any later version (`GPL-2.0-or-later`).

The current Deepwyrm codebase retains `GPL-2.0-or-later` across all components. Future components may use `GPL-3.0-or-later` only when the component's copyright and dependency provenance permits it and the component is explicitly marked according to `LICENSING.md`.

Full license texts are provided in:

- `LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt`
- `LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt`

When a file or component carries an explicit SPDX identifier or package license declaration, that specific declaration controls for that file or component. Otherwise the repository default above applies.
